INSERT INTO `mod_forever_journal_lore` (`ID`, `Zone`, `Kind`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `Races`, `Classes`, `Era`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(148000, 148, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Darkshore', 'Darkshore is a long, misty coast on the north-western edge of Kalimdor, a strip of dark forest and grey beaches between the mountains and the sea. Before the Sundering it lay on the shore of the Well of Eternity, and the ruins of Highborne towns still stand among its trees. Its only real town is Auberdine, the harbour that links the night elves on Teldrassil with the mainland and with the human and dwarven kingdoms across the sea.\n\nThe forest is sick. Beyond the eastern mountains lies Felwood, and its corruption has crept down the rivers into Darkshore: the thistle bears have gone rabid, the Blackwood furbolgs have turned hostile, and satyrs feed on the magic of the old ruins. Greymist murlocs and naga hold the beaches, and great sea creatures keep washing up dead on the shore.\n\nOlder enemies have returned too. Cultists of the Twilight''s Hammer search the ruins for forgotten power, and a coven of warlocks called the Cult of the Dark Strand has gathered at a Highborne tower in the north. The druids, Sentinels and townsfolk of Auberdine are few, and they welcome any help that comes off the boats.', 'quests 6342, 6343 (ferry and hippogryphs to Rut''theran); page texts 358, 364 (towns on the shore of the Well of Eternity); quests 4762, 2118, 984, 954 descriptions; quests 3524, 4740, 4725; quests 944, 966 descriptions; pre-Cataclysm lore: Auberdine harbour and its boat to Menethil Harbor'),
(148001, 148, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Auberdine', 'A night elf village on Darkshore''s western coast, built of pale wood around a moonwell and an inn. Its docks send ferries to Rut''theran Village at the foot of Teldrassil and ships south to Menethil Harbor, and the hippogryph master Caylais Moonfeather keeps flights going to the World Tree. Dwarven smiths, miners and archaeologists of the Explorers'' League have settled here alongside the elves.\n\nThe village is run by its elder, Thundris Windweaver, and a village council, and defended by a handful of Sentinels under Elissa Starbreeze and Glynda Nal''Shea. It is not an easy place to live. Murlocs have sunk ships off the coast, the forest around the village is turning against it, and some of its people have already left for the safer lands of the Alliance.', 'quests 6342, 6343, 4761, 965, 4740 (Auberdine Village Council), 4812 (Auberdine moonwell), 982; quest 2139 reward text (people leaving for fortified lands); creatures 3841 Caylais Moonfeather, 6737 Innkeeper Shaussiy, 6297-6301 dwarven smiths and miners, 2913 Archaeologist Hollee; pre-Cataclysm lore: Auberdine-Menethil boat'),
(148002, 148, 1, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ameth''Aran', 'The ruins of a Highborne town east of the main road, south of Auberdine. In the days of Queen Azshara its people practised powerful magic freely here, and two great tablets among the stones still tell of its founding and its fall.\n\nThe town''s people never truly left. Their cursed and wailing spirits walk the ruins, still carrying the magical implements of their old lives, and they drive off anyone who comes to read the tablets. In the middle of the ruins an ancient flame, blue in colour, burns as it has since before the Sundering.', 'quests 953, 958 descriptions; quest 957 description (ancient flame); page texts 358, 359; creatures 2176 Cursed Highborne, 2177 Writhing Highborne, 2178 Wailing Highborne'),
(148003, 148, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Bashal''Aran', 'The twin of Ameth''Aran, a second ruined Highborne town to the east of Auberdine. Sprites, grells and satyrs have moved into it, and they feed on the magic that still lingers among the stones, growing stronger the longer they stay.\n\nThere is one place they will not go. On a small bluff at the western edge of the ruins stands a shrine wrapped in a strange blue light. It is a prison, and its prisoner, the spirit of the Highborne mage Asterion, has stared out between its pillars for more than a thousand years.', 'quest 954 description and reward text; quests 955, 956 descriptions and progress texts; creatures 2189 Vile Sprite, 2190 Wild Grell, 2212 Deth''ryll Satyr'),
(148004, 148, 1, 4, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Tower of Althalaxx', 'A tall elven tower in the north-east of Darkshore, standing apart from the old towns. Ten thousand years ago it was the home of Athrikus Narassin, the Highborne who governed Ameth''Aran and Bashal''Aran for Azshara.\n\nWarlocks have taken it over, a cult that calls itself the Dark Strand, with a satyr among their number. The weaker cultists keep to the grounds; the strongest are inside. Balthule Shadowstrike, sent from Auberdine to watch the tower, has not dared to leave his post in case he misses something.', 'quests 965, 966 descriptions; page texts 364, 361, 437 (Balthule''s letter, a foul satyr); creatures 2336 Dark Strand Fanatic, 3662 Delmanis the Hated'),
(148005, 148, 1, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ruins of Mathystra', 'Broken walls and toppled stones at Darkshore''s northern end, all that remains of Mathystra, once a great stronghold of the elves. Its glory has faded, but fragments of its magic remain in the relics scattered in the grass.\n\nOthers have found the place first. Naga of the Stormscale have come ashore and made the ruins their own, and the Twilight''s Hammer covets the old elven magic buried here. The Ancients of the Grove want the relics studied before the cult can make use of them.', 'quest 951 description and reward text; creatures 2179-2183 Stormscale naga, 7016 Lady Vespira; quest 944 (naga in Darkshore)'),
(148006, 148, 1, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Cliffspring Falls', 'A waterfall in the mountains east and a little north of Auberdine. A cave behind the falling water is the only place where certain rare mushrooms grow, and the alchemist Barithras Moonshade used to gather them there.\n\nThe Ancients warned him away. They sensed a new evil hiding in the cave, and they were right: naga and thugs of the Twilight''s Hammer have made it a den. That the two should turn up together, so far from the sea''s depths, troubles Onu more than either would alone.', 'quests 947, 948 descriptions and reward texts; quest 944 description (naga and Twilight''s Hammer); creatures 2339 Twilight Thug, 7017 Lord Sinslayer, 2179 Stormscale Wave Rider'),
(148007, 148, 1, 7, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Cliffspring River', 'The river that runs down from the mountains north of Auberdine and empties into the Mist''s Edge. A bridge crosses it just above its first waterfall.\n\nIts water is going bad. Blackwood furbolgs camp along its upper course, but Thundris Windweaver believes they are only the nearest cause of the taint, not the root of it. Samples drawn from the pool below the falls grow more putrid by the week, and the village fears the foul water will soon wash down to Auberdine itself.', 'quests 4762, 4763 descriptions and reward texts; quest 1002 (buzzbox near the bridge)'),
(148008, 148, 1, 8, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Grove of the Ancients', 'A grove close under the mountains in southern Darkshore, home to living trees, the Ancients, who are among the night elves'' oldest and wisest allies. A few elves keep a small post among them.\n\nThe Ancients feel what moves through the forest, and their warnings carry weight in Auberdine. Onu, an Ancient of Lore, watches over the grove. Druids pass through on the road south as well, among them Kerlonian Evershade, a Druid of the Claw so recently woken from the Emerald Dream that he keeps nodding off on his way to Ashenvale.', 'quests 947, 948 descriptions; creature 3616 Onu gossip; creatures 4194 Ullanna, 4195 Tiyani; quest 5321 description'),
(148009, 148, 1, 9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Master''s Glaive', 'A huge blade driven deep into the earth in southern Darkshore. The Ancients say it marks the place where one of the old lords of the earth fell long ago, impaled by the glaive. The lord is long dead, but slivers of his power may linger in the ground.\n\nThe Twilight''s Hammer has set up camp around it. Their disciples guard a tome written in an ancient hand, and the dryad Therylune, who wandered too close, had to hide among the rocks until someone came to lead her out.', 'quest 944 description and reward text; quests 949, 950 descriptions; quest 945 description; creature 2338 Twilight Disciple'),
(148010, 148, 1, 10, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Remtravel''s Excavation', 'A dig site in the south of Darkshore run by Prospector Remtravel of the Explorers'' League, a dwarf famous at the Ironforge academy for his discoveries. His team uncovered signs of a great and ancient society here.\n\nThen the golems came. Stone creatures burst out of the ground and overran the site, and his assistant Hollee ran to Auberdine for help. Remtravel stayed, apparently without noticing, still looking for his stone brush and the fossil he had promised the League.', 'quests 729, 731, 741 descriptions and reward texts; creatures 2156 Cracked Golem, 2157 Stone Behemoth'),
(148011, 148, 1, 11, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Blackwood Den', 'A cave in southern Darkshore, below the road, held by the strongest of the Blackwood furbolgs. Their ursas and shamans guard it.\n\nThe druid Volcor was wounded by the furbolgs and took shelter deep inside, where he could neither fight his way out alone nor be found by his friends. His companion Grimclaw waited by the road outside and carried word of him to Auberdine.', 'quests 993, 994, 995 descriptions and reward texts; creatures 2170 Blackwood Ursa, 2171 Blackwood Shaman'),
(148012, 148, 1, 12, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Mist''s Edge', 'The strait between Darkshore and Teldrassil, crossed every day by the ferries and hippogryphs from Auberdine. Its waters are cold and grey, and the Cliffspring River empties into it from the north.\n\nThe sea here has turned dangerous. Greymist murlocs camp along the beaches and raid the boats, and two ships, the Silver Dawning and the Mist Veil, lie wrecked off the coast north of Auberdine with their captains'' lockboxes still aboard. Giant threshers and sea turtles keep beaching themselves on the shore, and nobody yet knows why.', 'quest 4723 description (coast of the Mist''s Edge); quest 4762 description (Cliffspring River empties into the Mist''s Edge); quest 982 description; quests 3524, 4681 descriptions; quest 1141 (no boats going out since the murlocs)'),
(148030, 148, 2, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thundris Windweaver', 'The elder of Auberdine, who looks after the everyday affairs of the village and is known for his sound and fair judgement. He believes dark forces are pressing in on every side and that the whole village must keep watch.\n\nThundris knows corruption when he sees it. He has seen Felwood''s taint before, and he traces the poison in the Cliffspring River back over the mountains to it. He is just as wary of the past: he wants the relics carried by the Highborne spirits of Ameth''Aran gathered up and destroyed, so their magic can never be used again.', 'creature 3649 gossip; quest 4761 description and reward text; quests 4762, 4763 reward texts; quest 958 description and reward text'),
(148031, 148, 2, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Onu', 'An Ancient of Lore of the Grove of the Ancients, a great tree who speaks slowly and only after long thought. Those who seek him out are told to listen to what the wind whispers.\n\nOnu was the first to put the Twilight''s Hammer''s presence in Darkshore together with the naga''s. He sends trusted helpers to the Master''s Glaive and the Ruins of Mathystra, gives them phials of scrying so they can speak to him from afar, and meditates on what the cult intends.', 'creature 3616 gossip; quests 948, 944, 950, 951, 961 descriptions and reward texts'),
(148032, 148, 2, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Asterion', 'A Highborne mage who lived in Bashal''Aran when the Well of Eternity still stood, second only to the governor Athrikus Narassin. Something went wrong between them, and Athrikus bound Asterion''s spirit to a shrine with a moonstone seal.\n\nHe spent more than a thousand years in that prison, sharp-tongued and half afraid he had gone mad. The seal was found on one of the satyrs of Bashal''Aran and destroyed in the ancient flame of Ameth''Aran, and Asterion is free at last. His first thought is of the world that has changed beyond recognition; his second is of vengeance on his former master, whom he senses is still alive.', 'quests 954, 955, 956, 957 descriptions, progress and reward texts; page text 365 (Asterion, second to Athrikus); item 5338 Ancient Moonstone Seal dropped by creature 2212 Deth''ryll Satyr'),
(148033, 148, 2, 4, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Athrikus Narassin', 'A Highborne favoured by Queen Azshara, who placed him over Ameth''Aran and Bashal''Aran. When the War of the Ancients brought the towns down, he came to the people of Ameth''Aran with a spell he said would protect them and give them eternal life. Their spirits still haunt the ruins.\n\nAthrikus survived the Sundering and leads the Cult of the Dark Strand from the top of his old tower, drawing power from soul gems that hold trapped Highborne souls. With those gems broken, he waits among his strongest warlocks.', 'page texts 364, 366, 367; quest 957 reward text (Athrikus still lives); quests 1140, 1167, 1143 descriptions'),
(148034, 148, 2, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Cerellean Whiteclaw', 'A druid of Auberdine who loved Anaya Dawnrunner of Ameth''Aran before the Sundering. After the battles at the Well of Eternity he heard that the town had fallen and that she was dead, and he followed Malfurion Stormrage into the long sleep of the druids with that grief still with him.\n\nThousands of years later, wandering the woods half in a daze, he came to the ruins and saw Anaya''s haunted spirit among them. He knows she must be released, but he cannot bring himself to raise a hand against her, and he asks someone else to do it and bring back her pendant.', 'quest 963 description, progress and reward texts; creature 3667 Anaya Dawnrunner'),
(148035, 148, 2, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Terenthis', 'A druid of the Cenarion Circle who has come to Auberdine to learn how far the fel moss has spread. Some of his brethren on Teldrassil had to be rescued from corrupted furbolgs, and he has vowed to stop such things happening again.\n\nHis scouts found the Blackwood furbolgs south of Auberdine already corrupted, and close enough to threaten the village. Terenthis does not like ordering the killing of forest creatures, but until a cure is found he believes there is no other choice.', 'creature 3693 gossip; quests 984, 985, 4761 descriptions and reward texts'),
(148036, 148, 2, 7, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Volcor and Grimclaw', 'Volcor is a friend of Terenthis who fell foul of the Blackwood furbolgs and lay hurt in their den. His faithful companion Grimclaw found Terenthis and brought the news, then went back to wait beside the road.\n\nTerenthis made an enchanted moonstalker cloak to let a rescuer slip past the furbolgs unseen. Once found, Volcor offered a choice: sneak out under the cloak''s magic, or fight down to the road and deal with the furbolgs once and for all.', 'quests 986, 993, 994, 995 descriptions and reward texts; creature 3695 Grimclaw'),
(148037, 148, 2, 8, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Tharnariun Treetender', 'A druid of Auberdine who has made the thistle bears his charge. Once noble animals, they have been struck by a sickness that leaves them rabid and destructive, and Tharnariun hoped to cure them, catching sick bears in a trap of light that calms them long enough to lead them home.\n\nThe cure failed. Grieving, he ordered the sick bears culled, and then the death of the Den Mother in her cave near Bashal''Aran, from which the rabid bears keep coming. He says plainly that many in Darkshore are not equal to the hardships of their new home.', 'quests 2118, 2138, 2139 descriptions and reward texts'),
(148038, 148, 2, 9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Wizbang Cranktoggle', 'A gnome inventor in Auberdine who has scattered his buzzboxes up and down the coast: lever-topped machines that let people talk to each other over long distances. Each needs constant repair, and he cleverly placed each one beside the creatures whose parts it needs, from crawler legs to thistle bear scalps.\n\nThe longer anyone talks to him through the boxes, the less sober he sounds. The buzzboxes also brew and distil liquor, a trade the night elves will not tolerate in their towns, and Wizbang hides a little of his best stock in them for whoever keeps them running.', 'quests 983, 1001, 1002, 1003 descriptions and reward texts'),
(148039, 148, 2, 10, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Murkdeep', 'A murloc of the Greymist tribe who guards a hutted camp on the water south of Auberdine. The village council holds him responsible for the death of at least one Sentinel, and suspects him of sinking two cargo ships off the coast.\n\nThe council has posted a bounty on him, payable by Sentinel Glynda Nal''Shea. Few things would let the people of Auberdine sleep more easily than news of his death.', 'quest 4740 description and reward text'),
(148040, 148, 2, 11, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Gelkak Gyromast', 'A self-styled pirate captain stranded on Darkshore''s far northern shore after threshadons sank his ship. He talks like a sea dog and calls everyone landlubber.\n\nGelkak''s pride is his first mate, the Threshwackonator 4100, a fighting machine stamped as his property. Its key broke on the rocks when he washed ashore, and crawlers, foreststriders and murlocs carried off the pieces. Once the machine is working again, he means to turn it on the murlocs.', 'quests 2098, 2078 descriptions and reward texts; creature 6669 The Threshwackonator 4100 gossip'),
(148050, 148, 3, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Twin Towns', 'Long ago the night elves, who called themselves the children of the stars, built their homes on the shores of the Well of Eternity, where they believed Elune herself rested. Of the towns on the shore that later became Darkshore, Ameth''Aran and Bashal''Aran were the finest, touched by Queen Azshara''s own hand and home to her favoured Highborne.\n\nAzshara gave the towns to Athrikus Narassin, who spent most of his days in the Tower of Althalaxx, and his second, the mage Asterion, saw to their people. The towns prospered while the world around them slid into madness.\n\nWhen the War of the Ancients came, the forest was torn up and the towns fell. As Ameth''Aran lay in ruins, Athrikus offered its survivors a spell of protection and eternal life against the Sundering to come. The Highborne spirits that wander its stones today show what that promise was worth.', 'page texts 358, 364, 365 (The Lay of Ameth''Aran); page texts 359, 366, 367 (The Fall of Ameth''Aran); quest 953 reward text; quests 957, 958'),
(148051, 148, 3, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Washed Ashore', 'Great sea creatures have always beached themselves on Darkshore now and then, but lately they come ashore in alarming numbers. The Temple of the Moon in Darnassus sent Gwennyth Bly''Leggonde to Auberdine to find out why, and the Explorers'' League tried to study one of the carcasses before murlocs chased them off.\n\nThe remains raise more questions than they answer. Some are threshers far larger than any native to these waters; others are gentle sea mammals and turtles from the seas around Teldrassil, which once swam in great numbers about the roots of Nordrassil and have grown scarcer since the new tree was planted. Gwennyth wonders whether they are fleeing the World Tree.\n\nSome of the turtles carried naga harness and cargo, marked with naga script, which explains the naga now on Darkshore''s northern beaches but not what they want.', 'quests 3524, 4681 descriptions and reward texts; quests 4723, 4728, 4732, 4733 reward texts; quests 4725, 4731 reward texts (naga carriages); quest 6343 (fish near Teldrassil larger than on the mainland)'),
(148052, 148, 3, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Taint from Felwood', 'Over the mountains east of Darkshore lies Felwood, a forest corrupted by demons, and its sickness is spreading west. The Cliffspring River is fouling, the thistle bears have gone rabid, and the Blackwood furbolgs, once friends of the elves, attack anyone near their camps.\n\nThe druids of Auberdine have learned that the furbolgs do not fall alone. Satyrs work their corruption through talismans, and when a cleansing offering of moonwell water and furbolg food briefly freed some of the Blackwood, a satyr corruptor came out of hiding to reclaim them.\n\nEvery victory so far has been small. No cure has been found for the bears or the furbolgs, and the elves can only slow the corruption until one is.', 'quests 4762, 4763 descriptions and reward texts; quests 2118, 2138 descriptions; quest 985 progress and reward texts; creature 10373 Xabraxxis'),
(148053, 148, 3, 4, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Twilight''s Hammer', 'The Twilight''s Hammer fought as an orcish clan in the Second War, and today it is a cult that worships the old lords of the earth, ancient powers defeated and imprisoned long ago. Its members have appeared in Darkshore at the Master''s Glaive, in the cave behind Cliffspring Falls and around the Ruins of Mathystra.\n\nA page torn from a tome at their camp turned out to be part of an ancient text written by elves, cursed and tainted by the cult''s own magic. The Ancients believe the Twilight''s Hammer means to use the old magic of the elves to call its masters back into the world, and are racing to understand that magic first.', 'quests 944, 947, 948, 950, 951 descriptions and reward texts; pre-Cataclysm lore: the Twilight''s Hammer clan and its Old God worship'),
(148054, 148, 3, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Cult of the Dark Strand', 'When Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze sent Balthule Shadowstrike to watch the Tower of Althalaxx, he found it full of warlocks whose scrolls named them the Cult of the Dark Strand, a group nobody had heard of. Balthule''s master, the paladin Delgren the Purifier at Maestra''s Post in Ashenvale, had suspected such a gathering.\n\nDelgren traced the cult''s strength to soul gems holding trapped Highborne souls, kept at Night Run and Satyrnaar in Ashenvale, and to its dealings with the orc warlock Ilkrud Magthrull of the Fire Scar Shrine. Behind it all stood Athrikus Narassin, the ancient Highborne lord of the tower.', 'quests 965, 966, 967, 970, 973, 1140, 1143 descriptions and reward texts; page texts 361, 437 (Balthule''s letter)'),
(148055, 148, 3, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Red Crystal', 'Moonkin roam the woods east of Auberdine in growing numbers. They were once thought gentle, almost mystical creatures, and some elves still revere them, but these attack on sight. Sentinel Glynda Nal''Shea learned they were gathering around a large red crystal on Darkshore''s eastern mountainside.\n\nMoonwell water poured over the crystal turned its surface clear for a moment, revealing fragments of bone and half of a humanoid jawbone sealed inside. Nobody knows what it is. Glynda suspects a link to Felwood, just over the mountains, and has taken the question to the village council.', 'quests 4811, 4812, 4813 descriptions and reward texts; creature 10158 Moonkin');
